\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,4) {$200$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,5) {$250$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,6) {$300$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,7) {$350$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,8) {$400$};
\node[below,font=\small] at (4.3,-0.9) {Number of units ($n$)};
\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-1.3,4.3) {Dollars (\$)};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,2) -- (8,6) node[pos=0.35,above left,font=\small] {$C = 100 + 2.5n$};
\draw[thick,red] (0,0) -- (8,8) node[pos=0.95,below right,font=\small] {$R = 5n$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use the graph to determine the break-even point in units and dollars, and state the profit or loss when $70$ smoothies are sold.

