\node[rotate=90,font=\small] at (-1.3,4.3) {Dollars (\$)};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,2) -- (8,6) node[pos=0.35,above left,font=\small] {$C = 100 + 2.5n$};
\draw[thick,red] (0,0) -- (8,8) node[pos=0.95,below right,font=\small] {$R = 5n$};
\draw[dashed,thick,black] (4,0) -- (4,4) -- (0,4);
\fill[black] (4,4) circle (3pt);
\node[above left,font=\small] at (4,4) {$(40, 200)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The lines intersect at $(40, 200)$.
Break-even point is $40$ smoothies at \$200.
At $n = 70$:
$R = 5(70) = 350$
$C = 100 + 2.5(70) = 275$
$P = R - C = 350 - 275 = 75$
Selling $70$ smoothies yields a profit of \$75.

